
# --- helpdesk vertical --------------------------------------------------------------
HELPDESK_STORE=/data/work/helpdesk/tickets.json

# Where a stopped run goes. This vertical needs it more than most: `propose` is built to hand
# a plan to a human, and the routing table it works from says "anything else is escalated for
# a human decision" — a promise that is only kept if the request reaches one.
#
# `.invalid` is the reserved TLD that can never resolve, so this default cannot quietly send a
# client's ticket subjects anywhere. Replace it, then `agent-alert --test`.
#
# `agent-status --ready` will report this deployment unfinished until it is replaced. That is
# the point, and it is not a defect in the example: a vertical can be complete while the
# deployment carrying it is not, and "who hears about a failure" is part of the deployment.
AGENT_RUN_ALERT_CMD=agent-alert
AGENT_ALERT_WEBHOOK=https://example.invalid/replace-me
